{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"normal-ludicrous-conure","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nADR 0122 adopts `amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0` for similar-ticket embeddings, and names the IAM gap as a deployment precondition rather than a follow-up. `infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf` grants `bedrock:InvokeModel` only for Anthropic Claude: the statement `ConverseAnthropicClaudeOnly` (`:10`) lists exactly two resource ARNs (`:16-17`), both `anthropic.claude-*`. A tree-wide search finds no Titan or embedding ARN anywhere under `infra/`. The embedding call is therefore denied from the Gerrit instance role today, so the index cannot be built anywhere but a developer's own credentials. ADR 0122 records that the benchmark missed this because it ran under a local principal that already had Titan access.\n\nThis blocks its sibling children: the index subsystem cannot run its embedding step in a deployed environment, and create-time surfacing cannot meet its production criteria, until this lands and is applied.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a **second, separately-named statement** to `data.aws_iam_policy_document.bedrock_converse` rather than widening the existing one. The existing statement's sid is literally `ConverseAnthropicClaudeOnly` and the file header (`:4-6`) states its intent as \"constraining the Anthropic model\"; appending a Titan ARN to that list would make both the sid and the header false, and would erase the Claude constraint that ADR 0059 records as deliberate (\"The region is wildcarded; the MODEL is not\"). A separate statement keeps the Claude constraint exactly as it is and makes the embedding grant independently readable and independently revocable.\n\nGrant `bedrock:InvokeModel` only. ADR 0059 records that `bedrock:Converse` was granted once on policy-simulator evidence and that a real call disproved it, and states the rule that granting an unused action is blast radius for nothing. Embeddings are a single non-streaming request/response, so `bedrock:InvokeModelWithResponseStream` is not granted either.\n\nScope the resource to one model ARN, `arn:aws:bedrock:*::foundation-model/amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0`, with the region field wildcarded for the same cross-region reason the Claude ARNs wildcard it (`:16`). No inference-profile ARN is added: a profile ARN exists for cross-region Converse routing, and the embedding call is a direct foundation-model invocation.\n\n**Verification is a real call, not a policy simulator.** `infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md` (\"How NOT to verify\") and ADR 0059 both record that the simulator answers what the policy language permits for the action you named, not which action the service actually checks, and that this exact inference was made wrongly once on this system. The attestation below is therefore an invocation from the instance role.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf` — add the `InvokeTitanEmbedding` statement.\n- `infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md` — record the second grant and that the embedding model is reached by direct foundation-model invocation, not a profile.\n- `docs/adr/0059-llm-provider-seam-and-support-tiers.md` — its IAM paragraph states \"IAM is scoped to Claude only\", which this change makes false; add a dated pointer to ADR 0122 and this ticket. The surrounding line citations in that paragraph (`iam_s7.tf:57-75`, `:60-63`, `:64-67`) are already stale against the present 26-line file and are left untouched rather than silently re-pointed, because correcting them is not this ticket's work.\n- `evals/similar-tickets/README.md` — `:131` states the review-bot instance role is not Titan-capable; update it to describe the grant once applied.\n\n## Testing\n\nNo automated test is added. Nothing in the tree asserts the policy document's shape — a tree-wide search for `ConverseAnthropicClaudeOnly` and `bedrock_converse` outside this file returns only prose in runbooks and ADRs — so there is no existing assertion to extend and a new one would pin a declared policy, not a live grant. ADR 0059 states the limitation directly: \"nothing verifies they were APPLIED before a change lands\", tracked as bug `1c39-96d4-8f9e-4d38`. A test asserting the HCL would therefore produce exactly the false confidence that bug describes. The real check is the live invocation recorded below.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf` contains a second statement granting `bedrock:InvokeModel` on `arn:aws:bedrock:*::foundation-model/amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0`, and the `ConverseAnthropicClaudeOnly` statement's actions and resources are byte-identical to their present values. Checked by: `git diff` on the merged commit showing the existing statement unchanged, and `grep -c titan-embed-text-v2 infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf` returning 1.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 on the change. Checked by: the recorded exit status, and Gerrit `Verified +1`.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The grant is applied and proven by a real Bedrock call from the Gerrit instance role, not a policy simulator: an `InvokeModel` against `amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0` returns an embedding vector. Attestation evidence recorded as a comment on this ticket: the Gerrit change number and submitted revision SHA, the UTC timestamp of the invocation, the returned vector's dimension count (expected 1,024 per ADR 0122), and the operator identity that ran it. Checked by: that comment existing with all four fields.\n- [ ] Documentation no longer claims the role is Claude-only: `docs/adr/0059-llm-provider-seam-and-support-tiers.md` carries a dated note pointing at ADR 0122 and this ticket, `infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md` describes both grants, and `evals/similar-tickets/README.md` no longer states the instance role cannot reach Titan. Checked by: grep for \"scoped to Claude only\" returning no unqualified claim, and each of the three files containing a reference to ADR 0122.","id":"f10f-c24a-3cfa-449e","parent_id":"4e89-30b9-1666-4e53","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Grant the Gerrit instance role InvokeModel on the Titan embedding model"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793578643054465871,"uuid":"42617126-1603-49a3-bb68-4fe350d3ee55"}